<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FictionBook xmlns="http://www.gribuser.ru/xml/fictionbook/2.0" xmlns:l="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">
  <description>
    <title-info>
      <genre>prose_classic</genre>
      <author><first-name>Fyodor</first-name><last-name>Dostoevsky</last-name></author>
      <book-title>White Nights</book-title>
      <lang>en</lang>
      <coverpage><image l:href="#cover.png"/></coverpage>
      <annotation><p>A sentimental novel from the diary of a dreamer.</p></annotation>
    </title-info>
  </description>
  <body>
    <section id="part1">
      <title><p>First Night</p></title>
      <epigraph><p>Was he ordained to live a moment close to your heart?</p><text-author>Ivan Turgenev</text-author></epigraph>
      <p>It was a wonderful night, such a night as is only possible when we are young, dear reader.<a l:href="#n1" type="note">[1]</a></p>
      <empty-line/>
      <poem><stanza><v>The sky was so starry,</v><v>so bright was the sky!</v></stanza></poem>
    </section>
    <section id="part2">
      <title><p>Second Night</p></title>
      <p>Well, so you have survived until tonight, she said, shaking both my hands warmly.</p>
    </section>
  </body>
  <body name="notes">
    <title><p>Footnotes</p></title>
    <section id="n1">
      <title><p>1</p></title>
      <p>Saint Petersburg white nights occur in June around the summer solstice.</p>
    </section>
  </body>
